2027-01-05T04:00:06  message   To the owner:
The one thing that makes a decline read as rude isn't the no, it's either a bare no or an over-explained one. So: be warm, be brief, don't invent a baroque excuse.

Warm and simple:
"Thanks so much for the invite — I'm going to have to pass this time, but I hope it's a good one. Have a lovely time and give my love to everyone."

If you'd like to see them separately:
"I can't make the party, sadly — but I'd love to see you properly soon, are you free for a coffee the following week?"

If you genuinely have a clash and want to say so:
