Simple practical question: red wine stain on cotton. Give real method.

Key: don't rub, blot. Salt while wet, or club soda. Cold water not hot (hot sets it). White wine trick is a folk remedy, dubious. Best actual: blot, cover with salt to absorb, then cold water and dish soap, or OxiClean/biological detergent soak. If dried, soak in cold water with enzyme detergent. Vinegar/baking soda myth.

Practical: 1) blot up, don't rub. 2) salt or cornstarch if still wet. 3) stretch over bowl, pour boiling water — actually that's a known method for red wine on cotton: stretch fabric over a bowl and pour boiling water from height. That works on cotton. Mention it as the classic one but caution it's for cotton only, fresh stains, and it can work well. 4) Or soak in cold water + detergent with enzymes, 30 min, then wash.

