What are the odds, roughly, of rolling at least one six on three dice?

2027-01-06T15:30:01  reasoning Reasoned (73 chars).
Three dice, at least one six: 1 - (5/6)^3 = 1 - 125/216 = 91/216 ≈ 42.1%.

2027-01-06T15:30:01  thought   (empty)

2027-01-06T15:30:01  message   To the owner:
About 42%. Comfortably under half, which is the bit people get wrong — three dice feels like it should be near certain.

The way to do it is backwards: the chance of no six on one die is 5/6, so on all three it's 5/6 cubed, which is 125/216, or 57.9%. Everything else is at least one six: 91/216, or 42.1%.

For company: one die is 17%, two dice 30.6%, four dice 51.8% — four is where it tips over even money.

