2027-01-06T16:47:36  thought   (empty)

2027-01-06T16:47:36  message   To the owner:
Eight minutes for a set-but-not-chalky yolk, nine if you want it fully firm. The grey ring is just overcooking — the sulphur in the white meets the iron in the yolk and that's what makes the green-grey edge. It's harmless, just dry.

The part that actually fixes it: cold water the moment they come out. Boiling water, eggs in, eight minutes from when it comes back to the boil, then straight into a bowl of cold water for a few minutes. That stops the cooking and pulls the sulphur away from the yolk.

And older eggs peel much more easily than fresh ones. If they're this week's, a pinch of baking soda in the water helps the shell let go.

Same answer I gave you on Monday, incidentally — eight and nine, ice water. If you're checking whether it stuck, it did.

