2027-01-07T18:51:46  message   To the owner:
Normal-ish, but it's at the edge. A phone in good health loses two to five percent on a normal night; ten percent means something is running in the background, or the battery has aged, or both.

Quickest things to check, in order of likely cause: battery health in settings — under about 85% and the loss is the battery itself, not anything you did. Then background app refresh and location services set to "always" for one or two apps, which is the usual culprit. Then whether the phone is sitting somewhere warm — overnight charging under a pillow or with a case on does this.

WhatsApp and anything with a live widget are the two most common drains overnight.

Rule of thumb: ten percent is worth a look, fifteen is a problem, five is nothing to mention.

Same answer as Tuesday's version of this. If it's dropped from five percent to ten recently, tell me the phone and I'll narrow it.

