2027-01-08T01:41:30  message   To the owner:
"Just checking in on the report — could you let me know where it's up to?"

That's the safe one. If you want to keep a nudge in it without the chill: "I may have missed it, but I don't seem to have the report yet — can you let me know when to expect it?"

The grumpiness comes from "per my last email", which says you've already had to ask once and are now keeping score, and from "again", which is the one that reads as a complaint. Drop both and you've got a question rather than a charge sheet.

What I wouldn't do is soften it to "when you get a chance", which is how a late report becomes next week's late report. Keep a date in it if you have one — "by Friday" does more work than any amount of politeness.

