Standard answer: blot, don't rub, with cold water and salt or club soda; then cold water + liquid detergent soak; for dried, white wine or baking soda paste. Actually the classic is salt immediately, then cold water. Hydrogen peroxide for light fabrics (not with bleach-containing detergent). Biological washing powder. Time matters — it's now set if it's an old stain.

