KEEN-wah. Two syllables, stress on the first, and the W is silent.

It's a Spanish spelling of a Quechua word, "kinwa", and Spanish at the time didn't have a letter that matched the sound — so quinoa came out with a Q and an I that don't match how anyone in the Andes says it. Same trap as chipotle and jalapeño: the spelling was built for Spanish speakers, not for what the mouth actually does.

