Least washing up first.

Shakshuka, one pan. Soften an onion and a pepper in oil, add a tin of tomatoes and cumin, simmer ten minutes, crack four eggs into wells, lid on for five. Eat from the pan with bread. One pan, one knife, one board.

Omelette, one pan and a fork. Three eggs beaten, butter, high heat for thirty seconds, drag the set edges in, fold, done. If you've got cheese or herbs, they go in before the fold.

