2027-01-08T20:31:26  message   To the owner:
The twenty-minute tidy, same shape as Monday's.

Minutes 1-5: take every bit of rubbish and every dirty cup to the kitchen. Nothing else. It's the fastest visible change per minute you'll ever get.

Minutes 6-12: one surface — the one you look at most from where you sit. Clear it completely, put back only what lives there, and put the rest in a single pile to deal with later.

Minutes 13-18: the floor. Anything on it that doesn't belong goes in the pile; then a quick sweep or vacuum of the middle of the room only, not the corners.

Minutes 19-20: deal with the pile. Half of it goes in the bin or away, the rest goes in a box out of sight.

The rule that makes it work: one room, and you're not reorganising anything, only moving things back to where they already live. If you start sorting a drawer you've lost.

