2027-01-08T21:03:41  message   To the owner:
Couple of options, depending on which way you want to lean.

Neutral and easy to act on: "Could you send the report over when you get a chance? It's running late again, so I wanted to check in."

Firmer but still polite, if this is the third time: "I think the report may have slipped past its due date again — is there anything blocking it on your end?"

The grumpiness in the original is doing two things: "per my last email" reads as a pointed reminder that they didn't answer, and "again" puts it on the record as a repeat offence. Both are fair, but they land harder if you drop them and let the facts do the work. "Is there anything blocking it" is the useful line — it's a question, it's cooperative, and it makes a non-answer awkward in a way you don't have to point out yourself.

