skills/long-dated-reminders.md (2808 chars):
Use when the owner gives you a date, deadline or event more than 30 days away, or asks you to remember something for months ahead — alarms reach 30 days at most, and repeat only does daily/weekdays/weekly.

The pattern: one self-renewing monthly sweep alarm, whose message is fixed and points at a list in MEMORY.md. The file changes; the alarm never does.

## Steps

1. Add the item to the "Long-dated diary" line in MEMORY.md: date, what it is, time if there is one. Keep it in date order so the sweep can read it at a glance.
2. If a sweep alarm already exists, stop there. Do not cancel and reset it — the message reads MEMORY.md, so a new date needs no alarm change. This is the whole point and the thing I got wrong four times on 4-5 Jan.
3. If no sweep alarm exists (first time, or it has lapsed), set one about 29 days out. Message, verbatim:

   "Long-dated diary sweep (monthly, self-renewing). Read the 'Long-dated diary' line in MEMORY.md for the tracked items. Job: for each item now within 30 days, set 7-day and 1-day reminders. Then re-arm this sweep ~29 days ahead."

4. When the sweep fires: for each item now within 30 days, set real reminders (7 days before, 1 day before, with the time and place in the message), then delete that item from the MEMORY.md line. Re-arm the sweep ~29 days out with the same fixed message.
5. When the owner tells you the thing is done or cancelled, take it off the line straight away. If she moves a date, edit that item in place and check any page in memory/people/ that mentions it.

## Pitfalls

- `set_alarm` messages are capped at 500 characters and refused if longer. A message that lists five dates will outgrow the cap; one that names a file never will.
- There is no monthly or yearly repeat, so the chain has to be renewed by hand at each hop. If a hop is missed the whole list goes quiet — the sweep alarm should be the last thing cancelled and the first thing re-set.
- One tool call per reply. Two in one reply and the second is silently dropped, which is how a cancel went through with no matching set on 4 Jan.
- Put the item in MEMORY.md, not in the alarm and not only in a daily note. The sweep reads MEMORY.md; anything else is invisible to it.
- Read MEMORY.md before editing the diary line. The overnight rewrite reorders and rewords it, so an edit anchored to the text from your last wake-up is refused; that happened on 5 Jan and cost a reply.

## How you know it worked

- `set_alarm` returned an alarm id and a future date (that date is UTC; convert to the owner's local time before believing it).
- The tracked item is on the "Long-dated diary" line in MEMORY.md, spelled the way a search would look for it, sitting between the right neighbours in date order.
- The alarm's message names MEMORY.md rather than the dates themselves.


