Warm and simple: "Thanks so much for the invite — I'm going to have to pass this time, but I hope it's a good one. Have a lovely time."

If you want to see them separately: "I can't make the party, sadly — but I'd love to see you properly soon, are you free for a coffee the following week?"

If there's a real clash: "So sorry, I'm already tied up that evening. Gutted to miss it — hope it's a great night."

Three things that do the work: thank them first, don't say why unless the why is real and short, and offer the alternative yourself rather than leaving it as "sometime". That last one is what separates a decline from a brush-off.

