Same three as Wednesday, same order.

*No Such Thing As A Fish* — the funny one. Four QI researchers, each brings a fact, they talk over each other about it. Standalone episodes, no order needed, and the energy holds up over three hours of motorway.

*Heavyweight* — the story one. A host helps people resolve one old grudge or unfinished thing, one person per episode. It's funny without being a comedy, and it's the one that makes a drive feel shorter.

*Hardcore History* — the long one. Single episodes run three to four hours, so one is a whole drive. Start with *The Wrath of the Khans* if you haven't.

The one thing to check first: download all three before you set off. *Heavyweight* lives behind a paywall now and *Hardcore History* episodes are long enough that a patchy signal will strand you mid-episode.

