2027-01-10T04:26:12  message   To the owner:
The grey ring is sulphur from the white meeting iron in the yolk — it's overcooking, and cooling too slowly. Both are fixable in the same thirty seconds.

Lower them into water that's already boiling, not cold water brought up to the boil. Six minutes gives you a set white and a yolk that's just fudged in the middle; nine to ten gives you fully set, no grey, if you move fast at the end.

Then straight into cold water — a bowl with ice if you have it — for at least three minutes. That stops the cooking dead. The grey ring forms in the minutes after you take the egg out, which is why it shows up even when the timing was right.

The one thing to check first: boiling water to start, ice water the second they come out. Timing alone won't save you.

