2027-01-10T04:56:48  message   To the owner:
About 42% — 91 in 216, if you want it exact.

The easy way round it: the chance of no six on one die is 5/6, so on three dice it's 5/6 × 5/6 × 5/6, which is 125/216. Everything that isn't that has at least one six: 1 − 125/216 = 91/216 ≈ 0.421.

So slightly worse than a coin flip, and much worse than most people guess. Worth knowing that at least one six on six dice is 1 − (5/6)^6 ≈ 66.5% — you need a surprising number of dice before it's a near-certainty.

