[Tue 05 Jan 2027 18:10] Owner: How do you pronounce 'quinoa' and why is it like that?

[Tue 05 Jan 2027 18:10] You: KEEN-wah. Two syllables, stress on the first.

The spelling has nothing to do with how it sounds because it isn't a Spanish word that got borrowed — it's Quechua, from the Andes, and it came to English through Spanish missionaries. Spanish writes the /ki/ sound as "qui" (think "queso"), and Quechua had no letter of its own for that vowel sound, so it got flattened into what you see. Nobody respelled it for English, so you're reading Spanish rules applied to a Quechua word.

Same family of confusion: "quinoa" and "Quito" start the same way. If it helps, the Spanish say KEEN-wah too — there's no secret version.

