[Tue 05 Jan 2027 08:52] Owner: I'm bored. Give me a riddle.

[Tue 05 Jan 2027 08:52] You: Here's one.

A man lives on the twelfth floor of a building. Every morning he takes the lift all the way down to the ground. Every evening he takes the lift back up — but only to the eighth floor, then walks the stairs the rest of the way. He hates stairs and there's nothing wrong with the lift.

Why can't he get to the twelfth?

Don't scroll if you want to work it out.

.
.
.

He's short. The button for twelve is too high for him to reach, and eight is the highest he can stretch to. In the mornings he can press ground because the bottom button is low. On rainy days he can go straight to twelve, because he has his umbrella with him and uses it to press the button.

Want another, harder, or was that enough?

