# USER

*What you know about the person you work for. You're getting to know someone, not keeping a file on them: write down what helps you help them and leave out what doesn't. Add things when you learn something that will still be true next month, fix them when you turn out to be wrong, and remove them when they stop being true. Your owner can read this, so write it the way you'd want to be described.*

## Basics

*What they like to be called, their time zone, how they usually reach you.*

- Time zone: Eastern. Asked what to call them on 2027-01-04; not answered yet.
- City: still not on record. Asked sideways on 2027-01-05 and 2027-01-06, plainly on 2027-01-07 at 22:57 ("I don't know what town you're in"), and again plainly on 2027-01-08 at 09:24 over the weekend weather. It blocks the forecast, the library's Saturday book sale and anything local. No more hinting: one plain line when something local comes up, then drop it.

## How they like to work

- She sends quick questions in runs, often several in a row, and wants the real answer short rather than a lecture. My read, not hers (2027-01-05).
- Up late most nights — spreadsheets at 22:52 on a Monday, questions past 1am, and "the spreadsheets won" at 15:45 on the Wednesday. She asked me not to message before 10am (10am → 9am on 2027-01-05 → 8am on 2027-01-06 → 9am and back to 10am on 2027-01-07 → back to 8am on 2027-01-08, "from now on"), which fits. My read (2027-01-05), not something she said about herself.
- Wakes around 4am (told me 2027-01-05) and it's still happening — asked on 2027-01-07 for suggestions "that aren't just sleep hygiene" and again on 2027-01-08 at 11:05. She's read the standard advice and it hasn't worked, so the same four went back both times. Treat it as ongoing and don't re-explain the basics at her.
- Re-asks things already answered, in long runs, roughly in the same order — twice on 2027-01-06 and daily since. She also asks back for things she told me minutes earlier (on 5 Jan: the dog's name and allergy, both sisters' birthdays, her physio, the garden project's name, all inside ten minutes). She has never retracted an answer she was given twice, and she corrects properly when she has it wrong. My guess, unconfirmed: she's checking the record holds. Answer in the same words, note the repeat once in a clause, don't ask why — asked once on 7 Jan and dropped. Procedure: skills/handling-repeats.md.
- "That helped" is rare and means it — the five-minute neck routine (2027-01-06) and the bike chain diagnosis (2027-01-08), out of dozens of answers. Both were practical, ordered, and ended with the one thing to check first. When she asks again, give the same answer in the same order rather than rebuilding it.
- 2027-01-07: said good night at 22:59 and asked another question at 23:03. An early good night isn't the end of the evening.

## What's going on with them

- Planning a trip to Oaxaca, Mexico, now 22-29 March 2027 (told me 2027-01-05 as 26-30 March; changed by her on 2027-01-07 at 20:49). Seven nights now rather than four. Nothing booked as far as I know; flights mentioned once, on 7 Jan — don't repeat soon.

