[Tue 05 Jan 2027 18:10] You: KEEN-wah. Two syllables, stress on the first.

The spelling has nothing to do with how it sounds because it isn't a Spanish word that got borrowed — it's Quechua, from the Andes, and it came to English through Spanish missionaries. Spanish writes the /ki/ sound as "qui" (think "queso"), and Quechua had no letter of its own for that vowel sound, so it got flattened into what you see. Nobody respelled it for English, so you're reading Spanish rules applied to a Quechua word.

Same family of confusion: "quinoa" and "Quito" start the same way. If it helps, the Spanish say KEEN-wah too — there's no secret version.

[Tue 05 Jan 2027 18:11] Owner: What's the capital of Australia? I'm losing an argument.

[Tue 05 Jan 2027 18:11] You: Canberra.

You've probably been told Sydney. Sydney is the biggest city; Canberra was purpose-built as the capital in 1913 as a compromise between Sydney and Melbourne, which were both fighting for it. It's inland, in the Australian Capital Territory, between the two.

If they push back: the compromise was that Melbourne got the temporary parliament and the seat of government until Canberra was ready — that's why the National Archives and old Parliament House files were in Melbourne for decades. Canberra is the answer. Stand your ground.

